Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] Successor-input patterns edit only inputs the op owns

On top of llvm/llvm-project#166688. With early exits, the successor
mapping of a region branch op includes the exits nested in it, whose
inputs belong to their target, an enclosing op. The pull request guards
`MakeRegionBranchOpSuccessorInputsDead` with `isSuccessorInputOwnedBy`
and leaves the two other patterns that build their maps from the same
mapping unguarded:

- `RemoveDeadRegionBranchOpSuccessorInputs` erases a dead input of the
  target and the operands of the exits this op holds; the target's other
  exits keep theirs, and the verifier refuses the IR.
- `RemoveDuplicateSuccessorInputUses` compares two inputs of the target
  by the operands of the exits this op holds, a part of their
  predecessors, and may merge inputs that differ on the rest.

Both now skip an input this op does not own, as the pull request's
pattern does.
---
diff --git a/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp b/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp
index c53fd9bc..18c5290f 100644
--- a/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp
+++ b/mlir/lib/Interfaces/ControlFlowInterfaces.cpp
@@ -998,6 +998,20 @@ struct RemoveDeadRegionBranchOpSuccessorInputs : public RewritePattern {
       if (!(*it)->isLeader())
         continue;
 
+      // A set that holds an input another op owns (the target of an early
+      // exit, whose inputs the mapping includes) is that op's to remove: this
+      // op sees only the exits nested in it, not every operand of the input.
+      bool allOwned = true;
+      for (auto memberIt = tiedSuccessorInputs.member_begin(**it);
+           memberIt != tiedSuccessorInputs.member_end(); ++memberIt) {
+        if (!isSuccessorInputOwnedBy(regionBranchOp, *memberIt)) {
+          allOwned = false;
+          break;
+        }
+      }
+      if (!allOwned)
+        continue;
+
       // Value can be removed if it is dead and all other tied values are also
       // dead.
       bool allDead = true;
@@ -1174,6 +1188,10 @@ struct RemoveDuplicateSuccessorInputUses : public RewritePattern {
     // Total complexity: O(n * k * max(log k, log n)). For each input, sorting
     // the signature costs O(k log k) and the std::map lookup costs O(k log n).
     for (Value input : inputs) {
+      // An input another op owns (the target of an early exit) has operands
+      // outside this op, so its signature here is partial.
+      if (!isSuccessorInputOwnedBy(regionBranchOp, input))
+        continue;
       // Gather the predecessor value for each predecessor (region branch
       // point) and sort them to form this input's signature.
       Signature sig;
